{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:93461","published":"2026-11-02T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-02T10:30:02.100888253Z","related":["CVE-2026-13595","CVE-2026-27456","CVE-2026-53612","CVE-2026-53613","CVE-2026-53614","CVE-2026-53615","CVE-2026-76642","CVE-2026-78408","CVE-2026-78410"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-13595","CVE-2026-27456","CVE-2026-53612","CVE-2026-53613","CVE-2026-53614","CVE-2026-53615","CVE-2026-76642","CVE-2026-78408","CVE-2026-78410"],"summary":"Important: util-linux security update","details":"The util-linux packages contain a large variety of low-level system utilities that are necessary for a Linux system to function. Among others, these include the fdisk configuration tool and the login program.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when setting up loop devices (CVE-2026-27456)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: heap use-after-free in libblkid nested partition probing (CVE-2026-13595)\n  * util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program via ancestor directory swap on target path (CVE-2026-53613)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when applying post-mount ownership/mode changes (CVE-2026-53612)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: SUID mount(8) allows nosuid/noexec bypass via LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 (CVE-2026-53614)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: failed external mount helper still runs privileged X-mount post-hooks (CVE-2026-76642)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: nsenter --join-cgroup leaks root cgroup migration authority (CVE-2026-78408)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: restricted bind mounts do not pin the source, allowing X-mount.owner/group/mode redirection (CVE-2026-78410)\n  * util-linux: util-linux: Partition metadata compromise via integer overflow in DOS partition parser (CVE-2026-53615)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":